# Title: PUA - Potential PE Metadata Tamper Using Rcedit
# ID: 0c92f2e6-f08f-4b73-9216-ecb0ca634689
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Micah Babinski
# Date: 2022-12-11
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1036.003, attack.t1036, attack.t1027.005, attack.t1027
# Description: Detects the use of rcedit to potentially alter executable PE metadata properties, which could conceal efforts to rename system utilities for defense evasion.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*OriginalFileName*" OR process_exec="*CompanyName*" OR process_exec="*FileDescription*" OR process_exec="*ProductName*" OR process_exec="*ProductVersion*" OR process_exec="*LegalCopyright*")) AND (process_exec="*--set-*") AND (((process_path="*\\rcedit-x64.exe" OR process_path="*\\rcedit-x86.exe")) OR (Description="Edit resources of exe") OR (Product="rcedit")))
